{"id": "swebq0048", "pool": "swebq", "tier": "balanced", "audio_s": 2.37, "n_chunks": 3, "n_concurrent": 3, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.1357, "eot_read_ms": 21, "reference_answer": "Indo-European languages", "query": "where does greek language come from?", "transcript": "Where does Greek language come from?", "mode": "local", "answer": "The Greek language comes from the ancient Greek civilization in Greece. It is one of the oldest recorded languages in the world, with written records going back over 3,400 years. Ancient Greek was spoken by the people of Greece and other parts of the Mediterranean region long before the Common Era. Over time, it evolved into different forms, such as Koine Greek, which became the common language of the Eastern Mediterranean during the Roman Empire, and later developed into Modern Greek. So, the roots of the Greek language are deeply tied to the history and culture of ancient Greece.", "answer_ms": 2845}
