{"id": "swebq0069", "pool": "swebq", "tier": "balanced", "audio_s": 2.32, "n_chunks": 3, "n_concurrent": 3, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.2625, "eot_read_ms": 20, "reference_answer": "In 1912, Lenin, who was forced to flee the country, chose him to serve on the first Central Committee of the Bolshevik party, which had now broken from the Social Democrats.", "query": "what led to stalin rise in power?", "transcript": "What led to Stalin's rise in power?", "mode": "local", "answer": "It was a long time ago in a big country called Russia. There was a man named Vladimir Ilyich Ulyanov, but everyone called him Lenin. After he died, another man took over his job. That man's name was Joseph Stalin. Stalin became very powerful because he promised to make the country strong and bring back honor after many hard times. He got support from soldiers and other important people who wanted change. Over time, he used that power to control everything in the country, so he stayed in charge for many years.", "answer_ms": 2542}
