{"id": "swebq0078", "pool": "swebq", "tier": "balanced", "audio_s": 2.46, "n_chunks": 3, "n_concurrent": 3, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.1926, "eot_read_ms": 20, "reference_answer": "School of Mathematics, Institute for Advanced Study;Humboldt University of Berlin Department of Physics", "query": "what colleges did albert einstein teach at?", "transcript": "What colleges did Albert Einstein teach at?", "mode": "local", "answer": "Albert Einstein taught at the Swiss Federal Institute of Technology Zurich from 1909 to 1911, and then he became a professor at the German University in Prague from 1911 to 1912. After that he worked at the German University in Zurich from 1912 to 1914, and later joined the Institute for Advanced Study in Princeton, New Jersey, where he remained until his death in 1955.", "answer_ms": 2124}
