{"id": "swebq0117", "pool": "swebq", "tier": "balanced", "audio_s": 2.09, "n_chunks": 3, "n_concurrent": 3, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.448, "eot_read_ms": 19, "reference_answer": "Mendelian inheritance", "query": "what was gregor mendel contribution?", "transcript": "Gregor Mendel's contribution?", "mode": "escalated", "relay": "Gregor Mendel is known as the father of genetics. His contribution was discovering the basic laws of heredity through pea plant experiments, including the law of segregation, independent assortment, and dominance. He showed that traits are passed from parents to offspring through discrete units, now called genes.", "expert_answer": "Gregor Mendel is known as the **father of genetics**. His contribution was discovering the basic laws of heredity through pea plant experiments, including:\n\n- **Law of Segregation**\n- **Law of Independent Assortment**\n- **Law of Dominance**\n\nHe showed that traits are passed from parents to offspring through discrete units, now called **genes**.", "expert_latency_s": 1.91, "stall_ms": 22, "relay_ms": 1282}
{"id": "swebq0120", "pool": "swebq", "tier": "balanced", "audio_s": 3.53, "n_chunks": 4, "n_concurrent": 4, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.3633, "eot_read_ms": 20, "reference_answer": "Government of Virginia", "query": "what was the government like in virginia colony?", "transcript": "What was the government like in Virginia colony?", "mode": "escalated", "relay": "Virginia had a **representative colonial government**.  It was led by a **royal governor** appointed by the English king after Virginia became a royal colony in 1624.  It had an elected assembly called the **House of Burgesses**, founded in 1619, which was the first representative legislature in the English colonies.  Only certain colonists, mainly free white male property owners, could vote or hold office.  Local government was often run by county courts and wealthy landowning elites.  So, Virginia’s government combined **royal control from England** with **some self-government through elected representatives**.", "expert_answer": "Virginia had a **representative colonial government**.\n\n- It was led by a **royal governor** appointed by the English king after Virginia became a royal colony in 1624.\n- It had an elected assembly called the **House of Burgesses**, founded in 1619, which was the first representative legislature in the English colonies.\n- Only certain colonists, mainly free white male property owners, could vote or hold office.\n- Local government was often run by county courts and wealthy landowning elites.\n\nSo, Virginia’s government combined **royal control from England** with **some self-government through elected representatives**.", "expert_latency_s": 3.05, "stall_ms": 24, "relay_ms": 3105}
{"id": "swebq0123", "pool": "swebq", "tier": "balanced", "audio_s": 2.92, "n_chunks": 3, "n_concurrent": 3, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.2483, "eot_read_ms": 20, "reference_answer": "Mathematician;Astronomer;Astrologer;Geographer;Philosopher", "query": "who was ptolemy and what did he do?", "transcript": "Who was Ptolemy, and what did he do?", "mode": "local", "answer": "Ptolemy was a great scholar. Every morning he would rise early and sit by the river to study the stars.", "answer_ms": 530}
