{"id": "swebq0132", "pool": "swebq", "tier": "balanced", "audio_s": 2.27, "n_chunks": 3, "n_concurrent": 3, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.144, "eot_read_ms": 21, "reference_answer": "Gare du Nord;Paris Orly Airport;Gare de Paris-Est;Paris-Gare de Lyon;Gare Saint-Lazare;Gare Routière Internationale;Charles de Gaulle Airport;Aeroport de Paris Beauvais Tille;Gare d'Austerlitz;Gare Montparnasse", "query": "what airport do you fly into in paris?", "transcript": "What airport do you fly into in Paris?", "mode": "local", "answer": "The main airport for Paris is Charles de Gaulle Airport. It's located about 20 kilometers northeast of the city center. If you're looking for a quieter option, you might also consider Orly Airport, which is closer to the city but serves fewer international flights. Both are well-connected by train and public transport.", "answer_ms": 1432}
