{"id": "swebq0168", "pool": "swebq", "tier": "balanced", "audio_s": 1.86, "n_chunks": 2, "n_concurrent": 2, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.1287, "eot_read_ms": 21, "reference_answer": "Zakāt;Salah;Hajj;Islamic dietary laws;Jihad;Sawm;Halal food;Shahada;Adab", "query": "what did the islamic people believe in?", "transcript": "What did the Islamic people believe in?", "mode": "local", "answer": "Islamic people believe in one God, Allah. They also believe in the teachings of the Prophet Muhammad, as recorded in the Quran. Muslims follow the Five Pillars of Islam, which include faith, prayer, charity, fasting during Ramadan, and pilgrimage to Mecca if possible. Their beliefs focus on living a righteous life guided by faith and community.", "answer_ms": 1604}
