{"id": "swebq0189", "pool": "swebq", "tier": "balanced", "audio_s": 2.55, "n_chunks": 3, "n_concurrent": 3, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.3831, "eot_read_ms": 21, "reference_answer": "Grand Canyon National Park Superintendent's Residence;Grand Canyon South Rim Ranger's Dormitory;Grand Canyon Village Historic District;Grand Canyon North Rim Headquarters;Grandview Mine;Grand Canyon Water Reclamation Plant;Buckey O'Neill Cabin;El Tovar Hotel;Grand Canyon Depot", "query": "what to see near grand canyon?", "transcript": "What to See Near Grand Canyon", "mode": "escalated", "relay": "Near the Grand Canyon, there are plenty of amazing sights! On the South Rim, you can't miss Mather Point for those classic canyon views, especially at sunrise. Yavapai Point and the Geology Museum offer great insights into the canyon's formation, while Desert View Watchtower is a historic spot with sweeping vistas. The Rim Trail is perfect for an easy walk along the edge. If you head north from Flagstaff or south toward Page, Arizona, Horseshoe Bend is one of the most famous nearby overlooks, showcasing the Colorado River in a dramatic curve. Antelope Canyon is another must-see slot canyon experience, though it requires guided tours. Lake Powell offers beautiful water-based recreation just a short drive away. And don't forget to check out some ancient ruins like Wupatki National Monument or explore the charming Route 66 town of Williams!", "expert_answer": "Here are top things to see near the Grand Canyon:\n\n### South Rim (most popular)\n- **Mather Point** – classic first viewpoint, great at sunrise.\n- **Yavapai Point & Geology Museum** – excellent canyon views and geology exhibits.\n- **Desert View Watchtower** – historic tower with wide views of the canyon and Colorado River.\n- **Rim Trail** – easy scenic walking path along the canyon edge.\n- **Hermit Road viewpoints** – includes Hopi Point, Mohave Point, and Pima Point.\n\n### Nearby natural attractions\n- **Horseshoe Bend** – famous Colorado River overlook near Page, Arizona.\n- **Antelope Canyon** – stunning slot canyon near Page; guided tours required.\n- **Lake Powell** – boating, kayaking, and scenic water views.\n- **Wupatki National Monument** – ancient Pueblo ruins north of Flagstaff.\n- **Sunset Crater Volcano National Monument** – volcanic landscape near Flagstaff.\n\n### North Rim area\n- **Bright Angel Point** – short walk to dramatic views.\n- **Cape Royal** – one of the best panoramic viewpoints.\n- **Point Imperial** – highest viewpoint in the park.\n\n### Towns and historic stops\n- **Williams, Arizona** – Route 66 town and Grand Canyon Railway.\n- **Flagstaff** – good base with restaurants, breweries, and nearby hikes.\n- **Cameron Trading Post** – historic stop with Native American art and food.\n\nIf you only have one extra day, the best nearby add-ons are **Horseshoe Bend and Antelope Canyon**.", "expert_latency_s": 10.21, "stall_ms": 24, "relay_ms": 4708}
