{"id": "swebq0195", "pool": "swebq", "tier": "balanced", "audio_s": 2.79, "n_chunks": 3, "n_concurrent": 3, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.2163, "eot_read_ms": 21, "reference_answer": "Greek Evangelical Church;The Church of Nails", "query": "what do christians believe about heaven hell and purgatory?", "transcript": "What do Christians believe about heaven, hell and purgatory?", "mode": "local", "answer": "Most Christians believe in heaven, hell, and purgatory. Heaven is where people go after they die if they have lived a good life and accepted Jesus as their savior. It's a place of eternal joy and peace with God. Hell is where people go who rejected God or lived sinful lives without repentance; it's often seen as a place of punishment and separation from God. Purgatory is the belief that some souls may go after death to be purified before entering heaven, especially those who loved God but still had some sin to overcome. Not all Christian groups agree on this last point—some traditions don't teach purgatory at all.", "answer_ms": 3353}
